{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1082,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Surely God is good to Israel, to those who are pure in heart.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3778},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1083,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"But as for me, my feet were almost gone. My steps had nearly slipped.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3781},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1084,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"For I was envious of the arrogant, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3784},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1085,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"For there are no struggles in their death, but their strength is firm.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3787},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1086,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"They are free from burdens of men, neither are they plagued like other men.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3790},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1087,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"Therefore pride is like a chain around their neck. Violence covers them like a garment.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3793},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1088,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Their eyes bulge with fat. Their minds pass the limits of conceit.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3796},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1089,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"They scoff and speak with malice. In arrogance, they threaten oppression.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3799},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1090,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"They have set their mouth in the heavens. Their tongue walks through the earth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3802},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1091,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"Therefore their people return to them, and they drink up waters of abundance.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3805},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1092,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"They say, “How does God know? Is there knowledge in the Most High?”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3808},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1093,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Behold, these are the wicked. Being always at ease, they increase in riches.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3811},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1094,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"Surely I have cleansed my heart in vain, and washed my hands in innocence,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3814},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1095,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"For all day long I have been plagued, and punished every morning.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3817},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1096,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"If I had said, “I will speak thus”, behold, I would have betrayed the generation of your children.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3820},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1097,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"When I tried to understand this, it was too painful for me—","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3823},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1098,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"until I entered God’s sanctuary, and considered their latter end.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3826},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1099,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"Surely you set them in slippery places. You throw them down to destruction.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3829},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1100,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"How they are suddenly destroyed! They are completely swept away with terrors.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3832},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1101,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"As a dream when one wakes up, so, Lord, when you awake, you will despise their fantasies.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3835},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1102,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"For my soul was grieved. I was embittered in my heart.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3838},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1103,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"I was so senseless and ignorant. I was a brute beast before you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3841},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1104,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"Nevertheless, I am continually with you. You have held my right hand.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3844},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1105,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"You will guide me with your counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3847},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1106,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"Whom do I have in heaven? There is no one on earth whom I desire besides you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3850},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1107,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"My flesh and my heart fails, but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3853},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1108,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"For, behold, those who are far from you shall perish. You have destroyed all those who are unfaithful to you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3856},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":73,"verse_ordinal":1109,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"But it is good for me to come close to God. I have made the Lord GOD my refuge, that I may tell of all your works.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3859}]}